  "full_text": "This is Temple OS 5-Minute Random Code walkthrough episode 47 and I'm your host Terry Davis. Here we go, Alt-B. We are in the song. We are in the song of Keeping. We are in the song. So this is a standard, this is a song that has graphics. This 8 is for the rating on a scale from 0 to 9. Keeping appears blue because, or green because it has graphics. Keeping is green because it has graphics. And it's an 8. The jukebox will change the number for you if you press. I can change it. Anyway, so we define a draw it callback. And that draws the heart. So, beat is based on tempo. So if I say T sub S, T sub S. This is time in seconds since boot. Beat is based on tempo. So this is the beat and it's synchronized to the music clock. The music clock is slightly different from the standard clock. It has some small delays. If you use T sub M, then this is slightly different from T sub S. Anyway, so we turn on transformation. We rotate about the Z axis. The Z comes out of the screen. So when we rotate about the Z axis, that's 0.2 radians. And we give it the rotation matrix off the device context. And then we dynamically scale it. We scale it by a factor of... We have 15 plus 1 divided by 15. So that's 16. Or 15 minus 1 is 14 divided by 15. Anyway, so... It beats slightly. If you want to see it again... Control-Alt-C... I can use Control-Alt-C because I set up Tribe Catch. And I put the settings outside. So that's that.",
